            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TROXEL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love the secret ingredient – peas. I now make this regularly, but do a couple of things differently - personal preference. I use 1 egg plus 2 egg whites, 2 scallions instead of 1. I also add ½ tsp soy sauce. Dark sesame oil is a must - use about 3 drops. This is a quick, delicious meal for one."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cindy Bonner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added quite a few more veggies, but in small amounts, one thinly sliced mushroom, a few thin slices of carrots and celery. I par-boiled the carrots and celery in the chicken broth, added the sesame oil and peas. I also added a dash or two of soy sauce. It was pretty good, but for me, it was still just a little bland. I will keep making this and playing with small additions.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-19T19:27:11.320Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Spenner Frank"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Family loved this soup. It's easy to add peas, shredded carrots, mushrooms, water chestnuts or other veggies if your choice. I used low sodium broth. Definitely will make it again.",
            "datePublished": "2016-09-12T02:55:59.237Z"
          },
